   "text": "The drawing shows streptomycin, so I wrote the SMILES from the known structure of that antibiotic rather than deriving each stereocentre from the wedges. I did not check every wedge and hash against the SMILES atom by atom.\n\nThe drawing matches streptomycin's three units:\n- **Streptidine core:** a cyclohexane ring with two guanidine groups (N=C(N)N) and several hydroxyls, joined through an ether oxygen to the central sugar.\n- **Streptose unit:** a five-membered ring containing O, with a methyl group, a tertiary C\u2013OH carrying a CHO (aldehyde), and a glycosidic O linking it to the third unit.\n- **N-methyl-glucosamine unit:** a pyranose ring bearing CH2OH, two OH groups and an NHCH3 group.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1[C@@]([C@H]([C@@H](O1)O[C@@H]2[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]2O)O)N=C(N)N)O)N=C(N)N)O[C@H]3[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H](O3)CO)O)O)NC)(C=O)O"
